  "configuration_id": "config_049",
  "reason": "The current best configuration (config_037: scVI + ViT-L, avgpool, weighted, multiprofile; acc=0.706) establishes strong evidence that multiprofile, weighted fusion, avgpool aggregation, and a learned RNA encoder (scVI over PCA) all matter. However, the RNA encoder axis remains the largest source of uncertainty: we have only tested PCA and scVI, and scGPT—a fundamentally different generative pre-trained architecture—has never been evaluated in any experiment. Config_049 (scGPT + ViT-L, avgpool, weighted, multiprofile) isolates the RNA encoder choice while holding all other parameters at their best-known values, enabling a clean comparison against config_037. If scGPT matches or exceeds scVI, it opens a new promising direction; if it underperforms, it confirms scVI as the preferred encoder and reduces uncertainty about whether further gains require architectural changes beyond the encoder. Under a limited budget, resolving this key design axis is more informative than re-testing fusion or aggregation variants that already have consistent evidence."
}

